course: dictionary
lesson: 2137
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «The hens sleep in the coop at night.» Here a coop is a small house where birds are kept. «Sam had been cooped up indoors all week.» Here coop is a verb: to be cooped up means to be kept inside a small space for a long time.
explain: The clues are the words around the word. Hens, eggs and a shut door point to the animal house meaning. Feeling stuck and bored, with rain outside, points to the verb meaning. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Watch out for a third meaning. A co-op, also written coop, is a shop or business owned and run by its members. «The village co-op sells fresh eggs and bread.» The clue is that a shop sells things, not that animals live there. Same spelling, different world.
explain: A word can also change its form. Coops is the plural of coop. The verb changes too: coop up, cooped, cooping. «The farmer cooped the hens up before dark.» Cooped is the past tense, so the action happened earlier.
fact: A coop is a cage or small house where chickens or other birds are kept.
fact: To be cooped up means to be kept inside a small space for a long time.
fact: A co-op (also written coop) is a shop or business owned and run by its members.
fact: «Foxes hunt chickens because they are hungry; a stronger coop protects the hens better than anger.»
fact: Phrases to know: chicken coop, hen coop, cooped up, and fly the coop, which means escape or leave.
exercise: «The hens sleep in the coop at night.» What is a coop? | A shop run by its members | *A cage or small house where birds are kept | A type of hot drink | A long walk in the rain
exercise: «Sam had been cooped up indoors all week.» What does cooped up mean? | *Kept inside a small space for a long time | Sitting on a warm chair | Chasing a fox round the garden | Flying high above the trees
exercise: «The village co-op sells fresh eggs and bread.» What is a co-op? | A rainy day in the village | A wooden hen house | A bird that lays eggs | *A shop or business owned and run by its members
test: Why does the farmer make sure the coop is shut at night? | To let the hens fly away | So the hens can see the stars | *To keep the hens safe from foxes
test: «Mia had been cooped up all day, so she ran out into the park.» What does cooped up suggest? | Shopping at the co-op | Flying in the sky | Sleeping in a warm bed | *Stuck inside a small space for a long time
exam: «They decided to fly the coop when the gate was left open.» What does fly the coop mean? | Buy eggs at the shop | Learn to fly a plane | *Escape or leave | Build a new chicken coop
